§3  SAT TOKEN LIFECYCLE SECURITY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  SAT — Sovereign Authentication Token

  Lifecycle Phases:
  ─────────────────

  1. GENERATION
     └── Token format: SAT-{CONTEXT}-{SEQUENCE}-{TIMESTAMP_B36}
     └── Generated at process spawn (ANIMA Runtime)
     └── Cryptographically bound to PID and timestamp
     └── Entropy source: OS CSPRNG + φ-resonance seed

  2. BINDING
     └── Token bound to process context at spawn
     └── Every module import carries SAT token reference
     └── Token propagated through IntelligenceWire messages
     └── Cross-ecosystem translations carry origin SAT

  3. VALIDATION
     └── FORMA model validates token format and integrity
     └── Token expiry checked on every operation
     └── Replay attack prevention via timestamp+sequence
     └── Cross-process token sharing explicitly prohibited

  4. ROTATION
     └── Short-lived tokens: φ × 3600 seconds (~5832 seconds)
     └── Rotation triggered by SAEIS enforcement layer
     └── Graceful handoff — old token valid for 1 φ-cycle overlap
     └── Rotation events logged to sovereign audit trail

  5. REVOCATION
     └── Immediate revocation on security event detection
     └── Revocation propagated across all connected organisms
     └── Revoked tokens added to distributed blocklist
     └── FORMA validates against blocklist on every check


