§4  QUANTUM-RESISTANT CRYPTOGRAPHIC PRIMITIVES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Post-Quantum Readiness:
  ───────────────────────

  Nova Encryption includes quantum-resistant algorithm support:

  • CRYSTALS-Kyber (ML-KEM)    — Key encapsulation for registry auth
  • CRYSTALS-Dilithium (ML-DSA) — Digital signatures for package signing
  • SPHINCS+                    — Stateless hash-based signatures (fallback)
  • NTRU                       — Lattice-based encryption for sovereign bus

  Hybrid Mode (Current Default):
  ──────────────────────────────
  All cryptographic operations run in hybrid mode:
    Classical (Ed25519/X25519) + Post-Quantum (Kyber/Dilithium)
  Both must validate for operation to succeed.

  Migration Timeline:
  ───────────────────
  Phase 1: Hybrid mode (current) — classical + post-quantum
  Phase 2: Post-quantum primary, classical fallback
  Phase 3: Full post-quantum — classical algorithms deprecated


