§7  INCIDENT RESPONSE ORGANISM PROTOCOLS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Incident Severity Levels:
  ─────────────────────────
  φ⁴ CRITICAL  — Sovereign integrity compromise, full system response
  φ³ HIGH      — Package or registry breach, model integrity threat
  φ² MEDIUM    — Unauthorized access attempt, token anomaly
  φ¹ LOW       — Policy violation, non-critical anomaly
  φ⁰ INFO      — Audit event, compliance notification

  Response Protocol:
  ──────────────────

  1. DETECTION (SAEIS Layer)
     └── Threat identified by SAEIS monitoring
     └── FORMA model validates threat classification
     └── Alert dispatched via IntelligenceWire

  2. CONTAINMENT (Sandbox Layer)
     └── Affected process SAT tokens immediately revoked
     └── Compromised packages quarantined in sandbox
     └── Registry access for affected packages suspended
     └── Cross-ecosystem translations paused for affected scope

  3. ERADICATION (Organism Kernel)
     └── Compromised modules purged from module cache
     └── Affected container images pulled from registry
     └── Memory Palace segments containing threat data isolated
     └── Knowledge Graph edges from compromised nodes severed

  4. RECOVERY (SYNTHOS + LEXIS)
     └── Clean packages rebuilt from source via SYNTHOS
     └── Cross-ecosystem translations regenerated by LEXIS
     └── Registry integrity verified by FORMA
     └── SAT tokens reissued for recovered processes

  5. POST-INCIDENT (AURO)
     └── AURO analyzes attack vector and system response
     └── Architecture adjustments recommended
     └── MACHINA SECURITAS model updated
     └── Lessons encoded into organism immune memory


