§8  CROSS-ORGANISM RESONANCE SECURITY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  φ-Resonance Authentication:
  ───────────────────────────

  When multiple organism instances communicate, they authenticate via
  φ-resonance signatures — cryptographic proofs that incorporate the
  golden ratio constant as an entropy source:

  • φ-Signature = Ed25519_Sign(message || φ^n || timestamp)
  • n = organism instance sequence number
  • Verification requires knowledge of organism lineage

  Cross-Organism Security Rules:
  ──────────────────────────────
  1. No organism trusts another without φ-resonance handshake
  2. All inter-organism data encrypted with Nova encryption
  3. SAT tokens are NEVER shared across organism boundaries
  4. IntelligenceWire messages carry origin organism proof
  5. Cross-organism translations validated by both LEXIS instances
  6. FORMA validates compliance on both sides of any exchange

  Resonance Disruption Detection:
  ───────────────────────────────
  If φ-resonance deviates beyond threshold (|measured - φ| > 0.001):
    → Immediate quarantine of affected organism connection
    → SAEIS alert at φ³ (HIGH) severity
    → Manual verification required before reconnection


